---
// "Your plan follows you" band: the two-maps + resume-anywhere duo.
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">On the tracker, not your laptop</span>
    <h2 class="h2">Your plan follows you</h2>
    <p class="sub">The map is GitHub Issues, so the whole project isn't trapped in a local folder on one machine.</p>
    <div class="duo">
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="maps-row">
          <span class="mtab on"><span class="d"></span>checkout map</span>
          <span class="mtab off"><span class="d"></span>billing map</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Two maps, side by side</h3>
        <p>Run two important features as <b>two separate maps at once</b>, each with its own frontier and its own grilling. <b>Park one and switch to the other</b> whenever priorities move, then pick the first back up exactly where you left it, without the two colliding.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat b">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/><path d="M2 9h20"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Pick up on any machine</h3>
        <p>Because the whole plan lives on the Issues, <b>not in a local folder</b>, you can stop on your laptop and <b>resume on another computer</b>, or hand it to a teammate mid-flight. Nothing to sync, nothing to export, the tracker is the single source of truth.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
